values=[s['sumDrawPassMs'] for s in samples];cpu=[s['hostDrawEncodeWallMs'] for s in samples];summary={'runId':r['runId'],'revision':r['build']['revision'],'executableSha256':r['executableSha256'],'resolution':[r['window']['width'],r['window']['height']],'sampleCount':len(samples),'selection':'Present >=600; earlier samples excluded by explicit frame-count threshold','sumDrawPassMs':{'min':min(values),'median':statistics.median(values),'max':max(values)},'hostDrawEncodeWallMsMedian':statistics.median(cpu),'drawPassCountRange':[min(s['drawPasses'] for s in samples),max(s['drawPasses'] for s in samples)],'zeroDurationPasses':sum(s['zeroDurationPasses'] for s in samples),'timestampNanosecondCommonDivisorObserved':math.gcd(*(round(v*1e6) for s in samples for v in [s['sumDrawPassMs'],s['minDrawPassMs'],s['maxDrawPassMs']])),'evidence':str(a.run),'scope':samples[0]['scope'],'limitations':'Instrumented, screenshot-free run. Sum of pass durations is not full GPU frame duration or shader-only execution time. Observed timestamp granularity limits per-pass accuracy; host wall time is not CPU utilization. No display FPS or instrument-free performance claim.'};a.output.write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2)+'\n');print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
